/E (The first day began with an introduction to the structure of the event, followed by the unveiling of a fictional legal case. Participants were grouped, given roles, and were also given time to prepare their arguments, setting the stage for the courtroom simulation. It was a day of planning, interesting decisions, as well as conversations among participants! The first day set up for the real action of Day 2! )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (The second day brought the setup to life, as teams stepped into the roles of prosecution, defense, and jury, engaging in passionate arguments, cross-examinations, and deliberations. It was like a courtroom scene from a movie unfolding right before your eyes. Then, after assessing the enthusiasm, eloquence and sharpness of each participant, the brilliant winners were decided - K. Prachita and Amgoth Ajay Nayak.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
